The plate looks like a side plate of about 20 cm, and the food mound is roughly 8-9 cm across. It appears to be shredded hash browns topped with pico de gallo and green salsa.

I estimated a mound of about 150 g, made up of roughly 90 g of hash browns and 50 g of salsa and tomato. The hash browns are fried, so I put them at about 1.5 kcal/g, which gives roughly 135 kcal. The salsa and tomato add about 20 kcal, for a total near 160 kcal. Allowing for some oil, I rounded up to about 190 kcal.

